# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GoTrue (supabase/auth) on Clever Cloud (Docker runtime).
#
# PREREQUISITE: the `supabase_auth_admin` role must EXIST BEFORE the first
# start. GoTrue applies its DDL migrations at launch, but creates neither
# the database nor the `auth` schema. Since the managed PostgreSQL add-on does
# not allow role creation, this template assumes a dedicated plan opened by
# support, or CKE (non-HDS track only: beta, no HDS zone).
# See modules/supabase/reference/clever-cloud.md §0.
#
# Alternative to consider seriously BEFORE deploying this, on the
# NON-HDS track only: the Keycloak add-on, native to Clever Cloud, which avoids
# a container to operate. Keycloak exists in NO HDS zone: in HDS,
# authentication is rewritten in the application (path 1).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Latest version noted on 2026-10-24: v2.197.0. Check the current stable
# version before deploying:
#   curl -s https://api.github.com/repos/supabase/auth/releases/latest | jq -r .tag_name
# Never go with `latest` in production.
FROM supabase/auth:VERSION_TO_CHECK

# Set CC_DOCKER_EXPOSED_HTTP_PORT=9999 on the application.
EXPOSE 9999

# THE FIVE STRICTLY REQUIRED VARIABLES, and only five:
#
#   GOTRUE_DB_DRIVER=postgres
#   GOTRUE_DB_DATABASE_URL   connection as supabase_auth_admin
#   GOTRUE_JWT_SECRET        THE SAME as PostgREST, Storage and Realtime
#   API_EXTERNAL_URL         public URL of this service
#   GOTRUE_SITE_URL          default redirect destination
#
# TRAP ON GOTRUE_SITE_URL: it is not just a default redirect, it is an
# IMPLICIT ALLOW-LIST — any URI sharing the host is accepted as
# redirect_to. Set it to the real public URL, never to a localhost
# forgotten in production.
#
# CUSTOM ACCESS TOKEN HOOK — two verified traps:
#   1. The function must return THE WHOLE claims object. GoTrue
#      REPLACES the set of claims with the hook's output, it does not merge.
#      A function that returns only its business claims breaks every token.
#   2. supabase_auth_admin has by default NO rights on `public`. Grant it
#      USAGE on the schema holding the function, EXECUTE on the
#      function, then REVOKE execution from the client roles. If the hook reads
#      a table, it also needs SELECT *and a policy* if RLS is enabled.
#      Forgetting this returns HTTP 500 on every token issued: nobody
#      can log in any more, and nothing in the application logs says so.
#
# SMTP: without a custom SMTP, the e-mail templates cannot be changed on
# the entry-level plans. Check it before promising customised
# transactional e-mails.
CMD ["auth"]
